1
00:00:15,710 --> 00:00:20,250
This is the tale of two cats
who work part-time jobs.

2
00:00:21,950 --> 00:00:24,370
This is Chatorazawa Tapio.

3
00:00:25,440 --> 00:00:29,010
And this is Roshihara Kuehiko,
who will soon become his comrade-in-arms...

4
00:00:32,110 --> 00:00:35,390
The customers are waiting for me!

5
00:00:35,390 --> 00:00:38,270
The two of them may argue,
but they head to the battlefield together.

6
00:00:37,270 --> 00:00:38,560
No dents.

7
00:00:40,300 --> 00:00:42,150
Dodging a barrage of projectiles...

8
00:00:42,380 --> 00:00:43,020
Wait a second!

9
00:00:43,010 --> 00:00:44,990
...and charging through
a hail of soba noodles...

10
00:00:45,450 --> 00:00:47,800
...and sometimes, going to
the mountain to cut the grass...

11
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:48,960
Stop moving, you idiot!

12
00:00:48,960 --> 00:00:51,270
...and then, going to the river to clean...

13
00:00:51,270 --> 00:00:53,030
This is turning into a rhythm game.

14
00:00:53,350 --> 00:00:55,400
They face a series of rivals.

15
00:00:55,950 --> 00:00:57,630
Sukoyama-senpai.

16
00:00:58,180 --> 00:00:59,870
Jakonegawa-senpai.

17
00:01:00,440 --> 00:01:02,210
Alpine-senpai.

18
00:01:02,570 --> 00:01:04,160
Koumori-senpai.

19
00:01:04,780 --> 00:01:06,450
Kanihei-senpai.

20
00:01:07,280 --> 00:01:08,930
Matsuzaka-senpai.

21
00:01:09,970 --> 00:01:13,620
Abandoned by heaven,
they lose everything.

22
00:01:15,510 --> 00:01:19,470
They find a single ray
of light in the blackness.

23
00:01:24,490 --> 00:01:26,410
And while they don't exactly get along,

24
00:01:26,410 --> 00:01:27,730
they now respect one another.

25
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:32,470
These two charge across the battlefield.

26
00:01:33,360 --> 00:01:35,600
When on difficult top-secret missions,

27
00:01:35,980 --> 00:01:39,110
they overcome a wide range of obstacles.

28
00:01:39,300 --> 00:01:40,400
Ku-chan!

29
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:41,510
They're coming.

30
00:01:41,520 --> 00:01:42,880
And don't call me Ku-chan.

31
00:01:42,880 --> 00:01:44,350
The line ends here!

32
00:01:44,350 --> 00:01:45,080
Right here.

33
00:01:47,320 --> 00:01:49,050
And don't call me Kuppi.

34
00:01:49,050 --> 00:01:51,490
See you tomorrow, Kuppi!

35
00:01:52,520 --> 00:01:57,880
Eventually, the two of them become
warriors, as well as corporate wage slaves.

36
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:06,900
Is that about right?

37
00:02:08,770 --> 00:02:10,870
It's not great.

38
00:02:10,870 --> 00:02:13,520
You mixed up the names
of the bosses on the on-screens.

39
00:02:13,520 --> 00:02:16,610
And the lines for Cut 32 and 33 are reversed.

40
00:02:16,610 --> 00:02:17,570
Seriously?

41
00:02:16,700 --> 00:02:18,170
Director Resapanda!

42
00:02:18,170 --> 00:02:19,590
The final cut is ready!

43
00:02:19,590 --> 00:02:21,180
Coming. Let me see.

44
00:02:21,780 --> 00:02:22,980
My name is Wooser—

45
00:02:22,980 --> 00:02:24,930
That's a different character entirely.

46
00:02:24,930 --> 00:02:25,790
Start over.

47
00:02:26,460 --> 00:02:28,540
It's not how we scripted it,

48
00:02:28,540 --> 00:02:30,360
but let's drop the weird yellow thing.

49
00:02:30,360 --> 00:02:31,980
It's a good way to end
but people are sick of it.

50
00:02:31,980 --> 00:02:34,330
We need a new gimmick for the new season.

51
00:02:34,330 --> 00:02:35,930
And anyway...

52
00:02:34,620 --> 00:02:35,930
This is hard.

53
00:02:40,430 --> 00:02:42,340
I'm done, Rac— I mean, Director Resapanda!

54
00:02:42,660 --> 00:02:44,320
You almost called me a raccoon, didn't you?

55
00:02:43,690 --> 00:02:44,530
No...

56
00:02:44,320 --> 00:02:46,030
I'll check it later. Just sit and wait!

57
00:02:46,030 --> 00:02:47,280
Yes, sir!

58
00:02:46,040 --> 00:02:48,720
Masked Palm Cive—
I mean, Director Resapanda!

59
00:02:48,720 --> 00:02:50,880
You just called me a masked
palm civet, didn't you?! You did!

60
00:02:50,880 --> 00:02:52,880
I called you Director Resapanda.

61
00:02:52,880 --> 00:02:53,740
I'm do—

62
00:02:54,090 --> 00:02:55,750
I didn't say anything.

63
00:03:00,620 --> 00:03:02,740
Yeah, looking good.

64
00:03:02,740 --> 00:03:05,690
So we're done now... right?

65
00:03:07,630 --> 00:03:11,400
But the ending's weak,
so let's put the weird thing back in.

66
00:03:11,400 --> 00:03:12,540
This will never end...

67
00:03:12,540 --> 00:03:14,510
My name is...